<title>ARGENTINA: Foreign holdings in Argentine assets at $16.94 bln.</title>
<headline>Foreign holdings in Argentine assets at $16.94 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign holdings of stocks and bonds rose 0.8 percent in January from the previous month to a total $16.94 billion, Argentina's securities and exchange commission, the Comision Nacional de Valores, said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Holdings in stocks by foreign investors stood at $7.13 billion at the end of January and at $9.73 billion for bonds, said the commission.</p>
<p>The main foreign investors in Argentine assets remained the United States, Britain and Belgium.</p>
<p>((--Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668))</p>
